.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T01:45:01Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T01:45:01Z","body":"My attempt was to take the materialx and turn it into glsl shaders https://github.com/V-Sekai/godot-mtlx it wasn't really working","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2914630831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2917324471","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106879#issuecomment-2917324471","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106879","id":2917324471,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6t4ta3","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-28T18:59:09Z","updated_at":"2025-05-28T18:59:09Z","body":"Importing now does not generate a visual shader but will instead generate two files `.vert.glsl` and `.frag.glsl` beside the imported file. Unfortunately, materialx's glsl gen is not compatible with compiling with vulkan (at least with the default flags) but this may be a more useful pivoting point than when we didn't have any glsl generation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2917324471/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993720244","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106879#issuecomment-2993720244","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106879","id":2993720244,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ycIu0","user":{"login":"ArchercatNEO","id":108980279,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn7oNw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108980279?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO","html_url":"https://github.com/ArchercatNEO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ArchercatNEO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-21T18:49:10Z","updated_at":"2025-06-21T18:49:10Z","body":"Update on why this hasn't been moving forward/what the issues actually are.\r\n\r\nThere are 2 ways to go about converting materialx into glsl inside of godot.\r\n* Use the materialx stdlib to convert from materialx xml directly into glsl then attempt to do something with that\r\n* Convert the materialx graph into a godot visual shader graph which will eventually turn into gdshader code and then glsl\r\n\r\nMethod 1 fails because most materialx materials use the [standard surface](https://autodesk.github.io/standard-surface/) shader model which is incompatible with godot's modified PBR shader model and naively attempting to treat materialx glsl as godot glsl causes immense problems. To solve this would require godot to support something like several shader models or just add a special case for standard surface. I do not know technically how much work it would entail but almost certainly far more work than just being able to read a shader graph.\r\n\r\nMethod 2 fails again because of standard surface. This time however instead of inscrutable vulkan errors we are faced with materials which just don't look quite right because the properties which standard surface provides are not the same as what godot expects leading to unused properties at best and broken materials at worst. Fire suggested that perhaps we could use an external program to turn standard surface shaders into openpbr shader which better align with godot's shader model. This could work but would still require an adapter and an external program to be useful. Overall this approach has lower implementation overhead but incurrs greater maintenance costs because we would need to bind every single node in the materialx standard library to an equivalent visual shader node whereas in method 1 only updating the library is required.\r\n\r\nOverall, what this PR has done is set up a structure to convert materialx nodes into visual shader nodes and convert a materialx graph into glsl. What is missing is that we require an adapter between the final materialx `surface_shader` and godot's shader model. That could come from either the godot shader model becoming more flexible to natively support surface_shader or through manipulating the surface shader until we can extract all information godot shaders can use from it. I am not currently qualified to do either or know the implications of either. If anyone would like to share an implementation which can convert standard surfaces to godot shaders it would greatly help this implementation.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2993720244/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]